msgid "Capacity followed by member buffer indices for each memory scope."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/transform/z3_scheduler/index.rst:111
msgid ""
"Stage-order constraints (u, w) requiring k_u <= k_w (same or earlier "
"iteration-stage)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/transform/z3_scheduler/index.rst:114
msgid "Recompute the minimum version counts from the selected schedule."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/transform/z3_scheduler/index.rst:116
msgid ""
"When False, constrain each resource so that, among the tasks using that "
"resource (pipe bit in resource_flags), max(start_time) - min(start_time) < "
"II. This keeps all tasks on a resource within a single II window (no "
"offsetting a resource's tasks across pipeline stages). When True, no such "
"constraint is added. Defaults to False (constraint applied)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/transform/z3_scheduler/index.rst:122
msgid ""
"Frontend stages for tasks in source order. Used only when "
"``manual_schedule`` is True; omitted entries are not allowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/transform/z3_scheduler/index.rst:125
msgid ""
"Preserve source issue order independently on every hardware pipe and "
"constrain every task's Z3 stage to the corresponding ``manual_stages`` entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/transform/z3_scheduler/index.rst:129
msgid "Z3 random seed; ``None`` leaves the solver default unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/transform/z3_scheduler/index.rst:131
msgid "Print solver inputs, search progress, and the selected schedule."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/transform/z3_scheduler/index.rst:134
msgid ""
"start_times: Start time for each task buffer_versions: Number of versions "
"for each buffer minimal_II: The minimal initiation interval found"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/transform/z3_scheduler/index.rst:144
msgid ""
"This function accepts TVM containers and converts them to Python lists. "
"Dependency arrays are ordered as directed data dependencies, resource "
"exclusions, shared-storage owner exclusions, and source pipe ordering. "
"``memory_groups`` contains ``[capacity, idx0, idx1, ...]`` entries; "
"``stage_order_deps`` contains ``(u, w)`` constraints requiring ``k_u <= "
"k_w``. The remaining arguments carry the loop's offset and manual-stage "
"policy from C++."
msgstr ""
